commit e7fbb767bf2baa23b5c42aa8ec7a5e355569b324
Author: Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 28 10:09:39 2026 -0600

    fix: copied-camp review — implementation review round 4 (Claude + Codex)
    
    - Open Studio inputs reset to their template ("Open Studio") on every editor opening — they used to
      keep the previous camp's text for any day the next camp doesn't store, and Save wrote it (pre-existing,
      now also reached by "Save & mark reviewed") (Codex 2, Claude 3)
    - "Save & mark reviewed" waits until the co-teacher list has loaded: Save omits sharedWith until then,
      so a box ticked late would be on screen but unsaved (Codex 1)
    - a Save that stops (no name, declined rename, error) re-queues the grid auto-save it had cancelled,
      so typing isn't dropped (Claude 1); a declined rename under "Save & mark reviewed" now says nothing
      was marked (Claude 2)
    - production check (fresh local backup, 2026-09-28T16:03Z): all 23 copied 2027 camps store every weekday
      for block1-3 + openStudio, no other block keys, no co-teachers — so a review sweep rewrites exactly
      what is stored (Claude 3's pre-ship check)
    - tests: failed save keeps the typing (auto-save) and stays unreviewed; co-teacher wait; Open Studio
      template per camp. e2e 145/145.
    
    Not taken: a timeout for Save's own wait on a hung offline write (pre-existing Save behaviour, same lock
    as before this feature — Codex 3 / Claude 4).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

